Wrote the design report to `review/opencode_looks.md`.

It includes:
- A blunt critique of the 5 current idle styles (plain/dot/arc/battery/clock) and the visualizer/gradient issues, grounded in the actual `EdgeView.kt` drawing values.
- 8 new premium idle designs (~48 dp quarter-circle bean) with polar-geometry specs from the screen corner, stroke/size in dp, accent/black color rules, cheap motion constraints, and conveyed information (recommends shipping: **Glyph Notch**, **Braun Meter**, **Mono Pulse Core**, **Eclipse**).
- 8 shape-fill/material styles to replace/complement the muddy radial gradient, each with an exact cheap Android Canvas recipe (`BitmapShader` tiles / cached paths/shaders), accent reaction, and perf cost — recommends shipping **Frosted Glass Tint**, **Concentric Grooves**, **Radial Sunburst**, **Radial Dot Matrix**.
- Precise, premium (non-tacky) music-beat mapping from bass/mid/high energy to closed-bean and open-panel properties with smoothing constants/limits (`τ=50–80ms`, scale capped at `+5%`, no whole-panel bounce/hue/rotation).
- A short panel design system (4dp spacing scale, icon/hit sizes, stroke widths, restricted accent usage, arc typography).

